WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
At any given moment, we 
humans have two choices

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.768
or&nbsp;two spirals that
 are available to us.

00:00:04.768 --> 00:00:06.609
The first is the
 toilet vortex.

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:08.059
The toilet vortex 
might start&nbsp;like this.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:09.452
You're picking on 
 yourself because

00:00:09.452 --> 00:00:10.707
you don't like the way 
you look in the mirror.

00:00:10.707 --> 00:00:12.437
You're&nbsp;unhappy with your 
level of productivity

00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:14.608
or you have failed to 
achieve ketosis, whatever.

00:00:14.608 --> 00:00:18.194
And then you take that 
out on other people

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.111
and then you are feeling
 more miserable,

00:00:22.111 --> 00:00:23.280
and&nbsp;then 
down you go.

00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:26.603
The vastly superior 
alternative is what

00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:29.062
I call the cheesy 
upward spiral.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.851
As your&nbsp;inner weather 
gets balmier,

00:00:30.851 --> 00:00:33.255
that shows up in your
relationships with other people.

00:00:33.255 --> 00:00:35.016
And because&nbsp;relationships are probably

00:00:35.016 --> 00:00:37.873
the most important variable when 
it comes to human flourishing,

00:00:37.873 --> 00:00:39.960
your inner weather improves even further

00:00:40.482 --> 00:00:43.350
and up you go. And that
 is the whole point&nbsp;here.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.667
Self-love, properly understood, 
not as narcissism,

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:50.803
but as having your own&nbsp;
back, is not selfish.

00:00:50.803 --> 00:00:52.852
It makes you better at 
loving other people.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.930
And that makes&nbsp;you more 
generous and more available.

